1. Introduction

This guide explains how to prepare a Kali Linux computer for building and running the Moderated Learning Management System (LMS). The project uses C++17, Qt 6 for the desktop interface, SQLite for data storage, CMake as the build system, and GoogleTest for automated unit testing where the test target is configured.

The instructions assume that the project source code and its CMakeLists.txt file are already available on the computer. Replace example directory names with the actual location of the project.

